      "provenance" = "4th-level spell descriptions - dispel illusion, the Evard black tentacles, the Leomund secure shelter, magic mirror, the Otiluke resilient sphere, shout, stoneskin and ultravision.  Pin-era pattern (R322): pinned data only - no engine site exists.  JUDGMENTs (the decode method): - the digit-garble family (the R343 precedent): the casting-time and duration 7s decode as 1 - the magic mirror \"7 hour\" as 1 hour and \"7 round/level\" as 1 round per level; the shout and stoneskin \"7 segment\" casting times as 1 segment. - the dispel illusion header loses its tail - only \"Dispel (Abjuration)\" prints; the name pins from the prose (dispel an illusion). Its stat block interleaves with secret page (R358-pinned) - the dispel cells pin as level 4, V S, 4 segments, half inch per level (the fraction cell prints garbled), permanent, none, special. - the Evard tentacles stat block prints a stray \"gf\" after the components and loses both the level and the range cells - the level pins from the section heading, the range is a hole pending the PDF. - the Leomund secure shelter prose scrambles the wind and strength sentences; the cells pin clean. - the magic mirror prose scrambles the component list (the hawk, eagle or roc eye; zinc, copper and nitric acid) and the spell-through list; the cells pin, the lists pin from the fragments. - the Otiluke sphere prose head is scrambled - the globe sentence is lost; the effect pins from the surviving tail. - the shout area cell prints 1 inch with the tail scrambled (\"x 3 cone\"); the prose pins the cone radiating from the mouth to a 3 inch terminus. - the stoneskin stat block loses the level and range cells (the level pins from the section heading; the range is a hole pending the PDF) and prints its components, casting time, save and area after the prose - an interleave. - the ultravision prose tail (the 3-foot radius sentence and the amethyst) prints past the 5th level heading; the cells pin clean. - the region also carries the R358-pinned secret page and sepia snake sigil bodies; their pins live in rules/ua/uamuspells3.h.",
    },
